    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0284" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 Recovery/6–2347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-23T17:00:00+03:00">June 23, 1947—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2246. Although apparent now that Molotov will participate in conversations in
                    Paris regarding a European economic plan, I feel sure that this participation
                    will be for destructive rather than constructive purposes. British and French
                    Ambassadors here have privately expressed same view to me. Reason for my opinion
                    is that intelligent and well implemented plan for economical recovery would
                    militate against the present Soviet political objectives.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d160-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d160-f1" n="1" xml:id="d160-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 2487, from Paris, not printed, Ambassador Caffery reported that
                    French officials feared that Molotov’s coming was designed to sabotage the
                    Marshall plan. (840.00/6–2347)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
